WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
The first film kept the protein cutters switched off until they reached the gut.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.780
Lipase, the fat cutter, needs no switch.

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.720
It is secreted already active.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.520
So why is fat the hardest of the three to digest?

5
00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.013
Look at one drop of fat in the gut.

6
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:23.253
Fat will not dissolve in the watery gut.

7
00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:27.433
So lipase reaches only the bonds at the drop's surface.

8
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:30.193
Every bond inside waits.

9
00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:34.767
Bile salts break the drop apart, the way soap cuts grease.

10
00:00:36.127 --> 00:00:38.607
One drop becomes a cloud of tiny droplets.

11
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:41.307
No bond has been cut yet.

12
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:43.927
This step is pure geometry.

13
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:50.110
Say bile splits one drop a millimeter across into droplets a micrometer across.

14
00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.530
The total amount of fat stays the same.

15
00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.890
How much more surface can lipase now reach?

16
00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:04.383
A thousand times more.

17
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:08.963
The same fat now spreads over a thousand times the surface.

18
00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:15.183
And the surface is exactly where lipase works, so far more bonds are within reach.

19
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:19.587
Now lipase cuts, helped by its partner colipase.

20
00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:24.587
It breaks the two outer ester bonds of each triacylglycerol.

21
00:01:25.787 --> 00:01:29.747
That leaves one monoacylglycerol and two free fatty acids.

22
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.270
Here is the one idea.

23
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.510
Lipase never needed switching on.

24
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:41.210
Its problem is reach: an active enzyme cuts only the bonds it can touch.

25
00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.390
So the gut's work on fat is exposure.

26
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:47.743
Reach matters again on the way in.

27
00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:52.203
Bile salts gather the pieces into micelles, tiny bundles.

28
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.783
The micelles ferry them through the watery layer to the gut cell.

29
00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.017
Inside the cell, the pieces are rebuilt into fat.

30
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:03.337
Why undo digestion?

31
00:02:04.777 --> 00:02:08.677
Rebuilding uses the pieces up as they arrive, so more keep flowing in.

32
00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:13.297
It also stops free fatty acids acting as detergents.

33
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.660
The rebuilt fat is wrapped in protein and shipped out as chylomicrons.

34
00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.060
Each one is far larger than the openings in a blood capillary's wall.

35
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:29.743
But at the center of each villus runs a lymph vessel, the lacteal, with loose

36
00:02:29.743 --> 00:02:35.263
junctions. Chylomicrons slip through and take the scenic route, through the lymph.

37
00:02:36.643 --> 00:02:39.483
Cholesterol and fat-soluble vitamins ride along.

38
00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.627
The other pieces need no detour.

39
00:02:44.027 --> 00:02:48.967
Sugars, amino acids, and short- and medium-chain fatty acids are water-soluble

40
00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:52.767
enough. They leave for the portal blood and the liver.

41
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:58.210
So, start to finish, the fat lane turns on access, not activation.

42
00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.210
Make surface for the cutter, ferry the pieces across, then find a door wide enough

43
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:04.730
to leave.
